Port of debian/patches/deepin-task385831-Defer-capture-start-on-Phytium-D3000M.patch
from PulseAudio: the initial snd_pcm_start() for capture is suppressed and
re-issued once a stream is actually recording.

The flag is delivered as the PULSE_DEFER_CAPTURE_START udev property, which is
mapped to the api.alsa.defer-capture-start node property. It is set by the
machine-specific udev rule distributed by the os-config package on matching
machines, and can also be provided through WirePlumber's monitor.alsa.rules.
